  "verbalization": "Quisqualic acid appears to exert its biological effects through a series of interconnected pathways, ultimately targeting DLD-1. The evidence suggests that Quisqualic acid acts as a target for 5-oxoprolinase, which in turn is a target of Lactucin and D-Aspartic Acid. This chain of targets leads to the final entity DLD-1, indicating a potential regulatory or enzymatic relationship between Quisqualic acid and DLD-1. The integration of these pathways implies that Quisqualic acid may influence DLD-1 through a series of enzymatic intermediates, possibly by modulating the activity of the enzymes involved in the pathway. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Quisqualic acid and DLD-1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
